# `.review/lens-stats.jsonl` is append-only: every /review round adds one line per dispatched
# lens, so two branches that both ran a review always differ at the file's tail, and git's
# line merge reports a conflict that is not a real disagreement. `union` is a built-in merge
# driver (no `git config` needed on a clone) that keeps both sides' lines. Each line is a
# self-contained JSON record, so the union is still valid JSONL; nothing relies on line order.
# GitHub's mergeability check ignores this attribute (community discussion #9288): a PR can
# still show CONFLICTING until the branch is rebased locally, where the driver applies.
# Not covered: `.review/attestations/` — content-addressed, one file per reviewed diff.
.review/lens-stats.jsonl  merge=union
